  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem. The nearest tickets are different. terminal#1504 is the original request for DLL/EXE icon paths with an index, which #14107 later implemented. terminal#19813 covers web URLs for icons, which were deliberately blocked. Neither covers indexed icons like `shell32.dll,210` being rejected by media-resource validation, or the first-comma versus last-comma parsing. Treat this as a new regression. Please go ahead with your fix: validate the binary path while keeping the signed index, split on the last comma in both the validator and IconPathConverter, and add the regression tests you listed. Until the fix ships, you can work around it by pointing the profile at a standalone .ico or .png file, or by using a path with no comma.\"}",
